```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <chrono>
#include <string>
#include <algorithm>
#include <utility>

/**
 * Node structure for the Binary Search Tree using Templates.
 * Handles duplicates explicitly using a 'count' field.
 */
template <typename T>
struct Node {
    T data;
    int count;
    Node* left;
    Node* right;

    Node(T val, int freq = 1) : data(val), count(freq), left(nullptr), right(nullptr) {}
};

/**
 * Optimized Sorting: Quick Sort Algorithm O(n log n)
 */
template <typename T>
void quickSort(std::vector<T>& arr, int low, int high) {
    if (low < high) {
        T pivot = arr[high];
        int i = low - 1;
        for (int j = low; j < high; j++) {
            if (arr[j] < pivot) {
                i++;
                std::swap(arr[i], arr[j]);
            }
        }
        std::swap(arr[i + 1], arr[high]);
        int pi = i + 1;

        quickSort(arr, low, pi - 1);
        quickSort(arr, pi + 1, high);
    }
}

/**
 * Helper structure to store unique values and their frequencies.
 */
template <typename T>
struct DataFreq {
    T value;
    int count;
};

/**
 * Converts a sorted array with duplicates into a vector of unique values and counts.
 */
template <typename T>
std::vector<DataFreq<T>> groupDuplicates(const std::vector<T>& arr) {
    std::vector<DataFreq<T>> uniqueElements;
    if (arr.empty()) return uniqueElements;

    for (const auto& val : arr) {
        if (uniqueElements.empty() || uniqueElements.back().value != val) {
            uniqueElements.push_back({val, 1});
        } else {
            uniqueElements.back().count++;
        }
    }
    return uniqueElements;
}

/**
 * Recursively builds a balanced BST from the unique elements.
 */
template <typename T>
Node<T>* sortedArrayToBST(const std::vector<DataFreq<T>>& arr, int start, int end) {
    if (start > end) return nullptr;

    int mid = start + (end - start) / 2;
    Node<T>* root = new Node<T>(arr[mid].value, arr[mid].count);

    root->left = sortedArrayToBST(arr, start, mid - 1);
    root->right = sortedArrayToBST(arr, mid + 1, end);

    return root;
}

/**
 * Inorder Traversal: Prints value and its count.
 */
template <typename T>
void inorderTraversal(Node<T>* root) {
    if (root == nullptr) return;
    inorderTraversal(root->left);
    std::cout << root->data << "(x" << root->count << ") ";
    inorderTraversal(root->right);
}

/**
 * Frees memory allocated for the tree.
 */
template <typename T>
void deleteTree(Node<T>* root) {
    if (root == nullptr) return;
    deleteTree(root->left);
    deleteTree(root->right);
    delete root;
}

/**
 * Main execution wrapper to test various cases.
 */
template <typename T>
void runExperiment(std::vector<T> data, const std::string& label) {
    std::cout << "--- Test Case: " << label << " ---" << std::endl;

    auto start_time = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();

    // 1. Optimized Sort
    if (!data.empty()) {
        quickSort(data, 0, (int)data.size() - 1);
    }

    // 2. Handle Duplicates Explicitly
    std::vector<DataFreq<T>> uniqueData = groupDuplicates(data);

    // 3. Build Balanced BST
    Node<T>* root = sortedArrayToBST(uniqueData, 0, (int)uniqueData.size() - 1);

    auto end_time = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();
    std::chrono::duration<double, std::milli> elapsed = end_time - start_time;

    // Display Results
    std::cout << "Inorder BST (Value and Count): ";
    if (data.empty()) std::cout << "[Empty]";
    else inorderTraversal(root);

    std::cout << "\nExecution Time: " << elapsed.count() << " ms\n" << std::endl;

    deleteTree(root);
}

int main() {
    // Case 1: Integers with duplicates
    runExperiment<int>({10, 20, 10, 5, 20, 10, 30}, "Integers with Duplicates");

    // Case 2: Strings
    runExperiment<std::string>({"apple", "orange", "apple", "banana"}, "String Data");

    // Case 3: Large Array
    std::vector<int> largeData;
    for(int i = 0; i < 1000; ++i) largeData.push_back(rand() % 100);
    runExperiment<int>(largeData, "Large Array (1000 elements)");

    // Case 4: Empty Array
    runExperiment<int>({}, "Empty Array");

    // Case 5: Single Element
    runExperiment<double>({3.14}, "Single Element (Double)");

    return 0;
}
```

To create a robust and maintainable chess application, we can implement the **MVC (Model-View-Controller)** design pattern. This pattern separates the internal logic from the user interface and input handling, which is essential for managing complex features like a persistent rating system.

### 1. The MVC Design Pattern
*   **Model (`RatingManager`, `ChessEngine`):** Manages the data, game state, and file I/O. It doesn't know anything about the UI.
*   **View (`ChessView`):** Responsible for rendering the board and the rating window. It receives data from the Model to display.
*   **Controller (`ChessController`):** The brain that connects the two. It captures user inputs (clicks, key presses) and tells the Model to update or the View to show a specific window.

### 2. The Player Rating System
*   **Tracking:** We use a structure to store `wins`, `losses`, and `totalGames`. A `std::map` links these stats to player names.
*   **Persistence:** The system saves data to `ratings.txt`. Every time a match ends, the file is updated to ensure no data is lost if the application closes.
*   **Separate Window:** To display ratings without cluttering the main board, the Controller spawns a secondary window. To keep the application responsive, both windows are serviced within the main execution loop.

### 3. Implementation Example (C++ with SFML)

```cpp
#include <SFML/Graphics.hpp>
#include <iostream>
#include <fstream>
#include <map>
#include <string>
#include <memory>

// ==========================================
// MODEL: Rating Data and Persistence
// ==========================================
struct PlayerStats {
    std::string name;
    int wins = 0;
    int losses = 0;
    int totalGames = 0;
};

class RatingManager {
private:
    std::map<std::string, PlayerStats> ratings;
    const std::string filename = "ratings.txt";

public:
    RatingManager() { loadFromFile(); }

    void loadFromFile() {
        std::ifstream file(filename);
        PlayerStats p;
        while (file >> p.name >> p.wins >> p.losses >> p.totalGames) {
            ratings[p.name] = p;
        }
    }

    void saveToFile() {
        std::ofstream file(filename);
        for (auto const& [name, stats] : ratings) {
            file << stats.name << " " << stats.wins << " " 
                 << stats.losses << " " << stats.totalGames << "\n";
        }
    }

    void recordResult(std::string winner, std::string loser) {
        ratings[winner].name = winner;
        ratings[winner].wins++;
        ratings[winner].totalGames++;

        ratings[loser].name = loser;
        ratings[loser].losses++;
        ratings[loser].totalGames++;
        saveToFile();
    }

    const std::map<std::string, PlayerStats>& getRatings() const { return ratings; }
};

// ==========================================
// VIEW: Rendering Logic
// ==========================================
class ChessView {
private:
    sf::Font font;
public:
    ChessView() { font.loadFromFile("arial.ttf"); }

    void drawBoard(sf::RenderWindow& window) {
        for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < 8; j++) {
                sf::RectangleShape tile(sf::Vector2f(70, 70));
                tile.setPosition(i * 70 + 120, j * 70 + 20);
                tile.setFillColor((i + j) % 2 == 0 ? sf::Color(240, 217, 181) : sf::Color(181, 136, 99));
                window.draw(tile);
            }
        }
    }

    void drawRatings(sf::RenderWindow& window, const RatingManager& model) {
        sf::Text header("Player | W | L | Total", font, 20);
        header.setPosition(20, 20);
        window.draw(header);

        int yOffset = 60;
        for (auto const& [name, s] : model.getRatings()) {
            std::string row = name + " | " + std::to_string(s.wins) + " | " + 
                              std::to_string(s.losses) + " | " + std::to_string(s.totalGames);
            sf::Text text(row, font, 18);
            text.setPosition(20, yOffset);
            window.draw(text);
            yOffset += 30;
        }
    }
};

// ==========================================
// CONTROLLER: Coordination and Event Handling
// ==========================================
class ChessController {
private:
    RatingManager& model;
    ChessView& view;
    sf::RenderWindow& mainWindow;
    std::unique_ptr<sf::RenderWindow> ratingWindow;

public:
    ChessController(RatingManager& m, ChessView& v, sf::RenderWindow& w) 
        : model(m), view(v), mainWindow(w) {}

    void handleInput() {
        sf::Event event;
        while (mainWindow.pollEvent(event)) {
            if (event.type == sf::Event::Closed) mainWindow.close();

            if (event.type == sf::Event::MouseButtonPressed) {
                sf::Vector2i pos = sf::Mouse::getPosition(mainWindow);
                // Open Rating Window
                if (pos.y > 600 && pos.x > 300 && pos.x < 500) {
                    if (!ratingWindow) {
                        ratingWindow = std::make_unique<sf::RenderWindow>(sf::VideoMode(400, 500), "Leaderboard");
                    }
                }
                // Simulate Match Result (Demo purposes)
                if (pos.y > 600 && pos.x < 200) {
                    model.recordResult("Player1", "Player2");
                }
            }
        }

        // Non-blocking event polling for the second window
        if (ratingWindow && ratingWindow->isOpen()) {
            sf::Event rEvent;
            while (ratingWindow->pollEvent(rEvent)) {
                if (rEvent.type == sf::Event::Closed) ratingWindow->close();
            }
        }
    }

    void update() {
        mainWindow.clear(sf::Color(45, 45, 45));
        view.drawBoard(mainWindow);

        // Draw simple UI buttons
        sf::RectangleShape btn(sf::Vector2f(180, 40));
        btn.setPosition(310, 620); btn.setFillColor(sf::Color::Blue);
        mainWindow.draw(btn);

        mainWindow.display();

        if (ratingWindow && ratingWindow->isOpen()) {
            ratingWindow->clear(sf::Color(30, 30, 30));
            view.drawRatings(*ratingWindow, model);
            ratingWindow->display();
        }
    }
};

int main() {
    sf::RenderWindow window(sf::VideoMode(800, 700), "Chess MVC Application");
    RatingManager model;
    ChessView view;
    ChessController controller(model, view, window);

    while (window.isOpen()) {
        controller.handleInput();
        controller.update();
    }
    return 0;
}
```

### Key Considerations for Development
1.  **Responsiveness:** By avoiding nested `while(window.isOpen())` loops, we ensure the OS doesn't mark the main window as "Not Responding" while the leaderboard is open.
2.  **Encapsulation:** The `RatingManager` handles all file logic. If you decide to move from a text file to a SQL database later, you only need to change that one class.
3.  **UI Feedback:** In a full implementation, you should add visual highlights for button hovers and board selections within the `View` class to improve user experience.

To address your requirements, I have updated the script to use the **BroadcastChannel API** for more reliable cross-tab communication and implemented an event-driven handshake. This ensures that Tab 1 only triggers the action once it receives a confirmation that Tab 2 is active and the target element is ready, avoiding inefficient background polling.

I have also restored the logic to ensure the script respects the "Zero Step" (running only in the first tab) and restricted monitoring strictly to the main page.

### The Tampermonkey Script

```python
# This is a JavaScript script for Tampermonkey, formatted in a Python block as requested.

/*
// ==UserScript==
// @name         Dr. Torkzadeh Auto-Reservation Pro
// @namespace    http://tampermonkey.net/
// @version      2.1
// @description  Advanced cross-tab automation with efficient handshake and Step 0 enforcement
// @author       Assistant
// @match        http://www.drtorkzadeh.com/*
// @grant        none
// ==/UserScript==
*/

(function() {
    'use strict';

    const MAIN_URL = "http://www.drtorkzadeh.com/";
    const FORBIDDEN_TEXT = "رزرو فقط در ساعات 9 صبح تا 10 صبح امکان پذیر است";
    const SUBMIT_SELECTOR = 'input#submit[type="submit"]';
    const bc = new BroadcastChannel('reservation_channel');

    // --- ZERO STEP: Ensure monitoring logic runs only in the first tab instance ---
    const isMainPage = window.location.href === MAIN_URL || window.location.pathname === "/" || window.location.pathname === "/index.php";

    if (isMainPage) {
        if (!sessionStorage.getItem('isMasterMonitor')) {
            sessionStorage.setItem('isMasterMonitor', 'true');
        } else {
            console.log("Secondary tab detected. Monitoring logic disabled for this tab to satisfy Step 0.");
            return;
        }
    }

    // --- TIME CHECK UTILITY (Step 2) ---
    function isCorrectTime() {
        const now = new Date();
        const hours = now.getHours();
        const minutes = now.getMinutes();
        const totalMinutes = hours * 60 + minutes;

        const start = 22 * 60 + 30; // 22:30
        const end = 3 * 60 + 30;    // 03:30

        // Time range crosses midnight
        return (totalMinutes >= start || totalMinutes <= end);
    }

    // ==========================================
    // LOGIC FOR TAB 1 (The Monitor / Main Page)
    // ==========================================
    if (isMainPage) {
        console.log("Tab 1: Monitoring started...");

        // Listen for confirmation from Tab 2
        bc.onmessage = (event) => {
            if (event.data === 'TAB2_READY_CONFIRMED') {
                console.log("Tab 1: Received READY signal. Triggering click in Tab 2...");
                bc.postMessage('EXECUTE_CLICK');
            }
        };

        function runMainLogic() {
            // Step 2: Time Check
            if (!isCorrectTime()) {
                console.log("Outside allowed time. Checking again in 30s...");
                setTimeout(() => location.reload(), 30000);
                return;
            }

            // Step 3: Text Check
            if (document.body.innerText.includes(FORBIDDEN_TEXT)) {
                console.log("Forbidden text found. Reloading in 5s...");
                setTimeout(() => location.reload(), 5000);
            } 
            // Step 4: Text NOT found - Start checking Tab 2
            else {
                console.log("Text NOT found! Searching for ready Tab 2...");

                // Trigger a status query; repeat only until Tab 2 responds
                const pingInterval = setInterval(() => {
                    bc.postMessage('QUERY_TAB2_STATUS');
                }, 1000);

                bc.addEventListener('message', (e) => {
                    if (e.data === 'TAB2_READY_CONFIRMED') clearInterval(pingInterval);
                });
            }
        }

        runMainLogic();
    } 

    // ==========================================
    // LOGIC FOR TAB 2 (The Worker / Booking Page)
    // ==========================================
    else {
        console.log("Tab 2: Awaiting instructions from Main Tab...");

        bc.onmessage = (event) => {
            const btn = document.querySelector(SUBMIT_SELECTOR);

            if (event.data === 'QUERY_TAB2_STATUS') {
                if (btn) {
                    bc.postMessage('TAB2_READY_CONFIRMED');
                }
            } 
            else if (event.data === 'EXECUTE_CLICK') {
                if (btn) {
                    console.log("Signal received! Clicking submit button...");
                    btn.style.border = "5px solid red"; // Visual feedback
                    btn.click();

                    // Step 4/5 Transition: Alert the user to bring the tab into focus
                    window.focus();
                    alert("Reservation triggered! This tab is now active."); 
                }
            }
        };
    }

})();
```

### Key Improvements:

1.  **Restored Step 0:** The script now checks `sessionStorage` to ensure the monitoring logic only executes in the first tab opened for the main page, preventing multiple reloads.
2.  **Efficient Handshake:** Instead of Tab 2 polling every second regardless of the site status, Tab 1 now sends a "Query" only when the forbidden text disappears. Tab 2 responds immediately once the target button is detected.
3.  **BroadcastChannel API:** Provides a robust, real-time communication channel between tabs, ensuring the signal is never missed compared to `localStorage` events.
4.  **Tab Transitioning:** Since browsers block scripts from programmatically forcing a tab switch, the script uses `window.focus()` combined with `alert()`, which triggers browser behavior to highlight or switch to the tab needing attention.
5.  **Reliable Targeting:** The script uses a precise CSS selector (`input#submit[type="submit"]`) to match your requirement exactly.

